# config/suricata/rp-soc.rules + notes — Suricata app-layer ICS signatures, PASSIVE local.
#
# Suricata is Apache-2.0. It runs passive on the SPAN mirror. ICS app-layer protocols
# (modbus / dnp3 / iec61850 / enip / bacnet) decode control traffic; local rule source only.
#
# INvariant (sec-verify check A/B): NO cloud signatures, NO external rule download, NO remote.
# ICS signatures are loaded from the co-op's own local rule set; no call-home.
#
# To enable in a co-op Suricata local rule set (e.g. /etc/suricata/local.rules):
#   include $RULES/ics-dnp3.rules
#   include $RULES/ics-modbus.rules
#   include $RULES/ics-iec61850.rules
#   include $RULES/ics-enip.rules
#   include $RULES/ics-bacnet.rules
#
# ICS signature sources (community, verify current + DRL attribution) — ICS-Security-Tools
# (DRL), Emerging Threats community rules (some under their own license; verify per-file),
# and open62541/lib60870/libiec61850-based parsers for offline replay/canary (NOT live egress).
#
# >>>>>>  No remote / no cloud / no external rule feed.  Local rule tarball only.  <<<<<<
#
# NOTE on copyleft: Suricata (Apache-2.0), lib60870 and libiec61850 (GPL-2.0/3.0-ish; check per
# repo SPDX). If the co-op builds a binary that links lib60870/libiec61850, that binary is GPL —
# keep it a separate INDEPENDENT binary in its own segmented VLAN, NOT linked into co-owned code.
